{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1768789443454,"sessionID":"ses_42bf06b73fferOyRzWXGUvK9Pd","part":{"id":"prt_bd411025e001Y5WJcBJUwFppJs","sessionID":"ses_42bf06b73fferOyRzWXGUvK9Pd","messageID":"msg_bd410f658001az6N2ApOIBGWhd","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_nljvl9yo7dgq_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/smaluk/dev/personal/chronotunes/node_modules/@convex-dev/presence/README.md"},"output":"<file>\n00001| # Presence Convex Component\n00002| \n00003| [![npm version](https://badge.fury.io/js/@convex-dev%2Fpresence.svg)](https://badge.fury.io/js/@convex-dev%2Fpresence)\n00004| \n00005| A Convex component for managing presence functionality, i.e., a live-updating\n00006| list of users in a \"room\" including their status for when they were last online.\n00007| \n00008| ![Demo of presence component](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/get-convex/presence/main/presence.gif)\n00009| \n00010| It can be tricky to implement presence efficiently, without any polling and\n00011| without re-running queries every time a user sends a heartbeat message. This\n00012| component implements presence via Convex scheduled functions such that clients\n00013| only receive updates when a user joins or leaves the room.\n00014| \n00015| The most common use case for this component is via the usePresence hook, which\n00016| takes care of sending heartbeart messages to the server and gracefully\n00017| disconnecting a user when the tab is closed.\n00018| \n00019| [![The Presence Component Video](https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZZTm_NtWJrs/0.jpg)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZZTm_NtWJrs)\n00020| \n00021| ## Installation\n00022| \n00023| ```bash\n00024| npm install @convex-dev/presence\n00025| ```\n00026| \n00027| ## Examples\n00028| \n00029| See the `example` directory for a simple example of how to use this component.\n00030| The `example-with-auth` directory shows how to use the component with\n00031| authentication.\n00032| \n00033| There's a hosted version of `example-with-auth` at\n00034| https://presence.previews.convex.dev.\n00035| \n00036| ## Usage\n00037| \n00038| First, add the component to your Convex app:\n00039| \n00040| `convex/convex.config.ts`\n00041| \n00042| ```ts\n00043| import { defineApp } from \"convex/server\";\n00044| import presence from \"@convex-dev/presence/convex.config.js\";\n00045| \n00046| const app = defineApp();\n00047| app.use(presence);\n00048| export default app;\n00049| ```\n00050| \n00051| `convex/presence.ts`\n00052| \n00053| ```ts\n00054| import { mutation, query } from \"./_generated/server\";\n00055| import { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\n00056| import { v } from \"convex/values\";\n00057| import { Presence } from \"@convex-dev/presence\";\n00058| \n00059| export const presence = new Presence(components.presence);\n00060| \n00061| export const heartbeat = mutation({\n00062|   args: {\n00063|     roomId: v.string(),\n00064|     userId: v.string(),\n00065|     sessionId: v.string(),\n00066|     interval: v.number(),\n00067|   },\n00068|   handler: async (ctx, { roomId, userId, sessionId, interval }) => {\n00069|     // TODO: Add your auth checks here.\n00070|     return await presence.heartbeat(ctx, roomId, userId, sessionId, interval);\n00071|   },\n00072| });\n00073| \n00074| export const list = query({\n00075|   args: { roomToken: v.string() },\n00076|   handler: async (ctx, { roomToken }) => {\n00077|     // Avoid adding per-user reads so all subscriptions can share same cache.\n00078|     return await presence.list(ctx, roomToken);\n00079|   },\n00080| });\n00081| \n00082| export const disconnect = mutation({\n00083|   args: { sessionToken: v.string() },\n00084|   handler: async (ctx, { sessionToken }) => {\n00085|     // Can't check auth here because it's called over http from sendBeacon.\n00086|     return await presence.disconnect(ctx, sessionToken);\n00087|   },\n00088| });\n00089| ```\n00090| \n00091| A `Presence` React component can be instantiated from your client code like\n00092| this:\n00093| \n00094| `src/App.tsx`\n00095| \n00096| ```tsx\n00097| import { api } from \"../convex/_generated/api\";\n00098| import usePresence from \"@convex-dev/presence/react\";\n00099| import FacePile from \"@convex-dev/presence/facepile\";\n00100| \n00101| export default function App(): React.ReactElement {\n00102|   const [name] = useState(() => \"User \" + Math.floor(Math.random() * 10000));\n00103|   const presenceState = usePresence(api.presence, \"my-chat-room\", name);\n00104| \n00105|   return (\n00106|     <main>\n00107|       <FacePile presenceState={presenceState ?? []} />\n00108|     </main>\n00109|   );\n00110| }\n00111| ```\n00112| \n00113| This uses the basic `FacePile` component included with this package but you can\n00114| easily copy this code and use the `usePresence` hook directly to implement your\n00115| own styling.\n00116| \n00117| ### React Native support\n00118| \n00119| If you're using React Native, install these optional dependencies:\n00120| \n00121| ```sh\n00122| npx expo install react-native expo-crypto\n00123| ```\n00124| \n00125| and then import the `usePresence` hook from `@convex-dev/presence/react-native`:\n00126| \n00127| ```ts\n00128| import { usePresence } from \"@convex-dev/presence/react-native\";\n00129| ```\n00130| \n00131| _Note: The <FacePile /> component currently doesn't have a React Native\n00132| equivalent, but you can easily create your own._\n00133| \n00134| ## Additional functionality\n00135| \n00136| The component interface for the `Presence` class is defined in\n00137| `src/client/index.ts`. It includes additional functions for maintaining presence\n00138| state and for querying presence for a given user or room.\n00139| \n00140| e.g., you can use the `listUser` function to check if a user is online in any\n00141| room.\n00142| \n00143| Reach out or join the [Convex Discord Community](https://convex.dev/community)\n00144| if you have any questions or feedback!\n00145| \n\n(End of file - total 145 lines)\n</file>","title":"node_modules/@convex-dev/presence/README.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Presence Convex Component\n\n[![npm version](https://badge.fury.io/js/@convex-dev%2Fpresence.svg)](https://badge.fury.io/js/@convex-dev%2Fpresence)\n\nA Convex component for managing presence functionality, i.e., a live-updating\nlist of users in a \"room\" including their status for when they were last online.\n\n![Demo of presence component](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/get-convex/presence/main/presence.gif)\n\nIt can be tricky to implement presence efficiently, without any polling and\nwithout re-running queries every time a user sends a heartbeat message. This\ncomponent implements presence via Convex scheduled functions such that clients\nonly receive updates when a user joins or leaves the room.\n\nThe most common use case for this component is via the usePresence hook, which\ntakes care of sending heartbeart messages to the server and gracefully\ndisconnecting a user when the tab is closed.\n\n[![The Presence Component Video](https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZZTm_NtWJrs/0.jpg)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZZTm_NtWJrs)\n","truncated":false},"time":{"start":1768789443452,"end":1768789443453}}}}
